From: PupJune2 <PupJune2@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 11:00:00 +0000
Subject: CromIKO Manga Mode

Add "Manga mode" to the app menu of web pages. The first time on a
site, it asks the user to tap the next chapter button, the previous
chapter button and a page of the chapter (either button can be
skipped), and saves how to find them for that site. Then chapters of
the site open in a full screen reader: only the chapter images, at full
width on black, with small buttons for the previous and the next
chapter at the top left and a close button at the top right. A tap
shows or hides the buttons and goes full screen.

The reader keeps the page and hides everything else, so the site's own
lazy loading keeps working while scrolling; images added later by the
site are laid out as they come, and images still waiting for the site's
script are started when they come near the screen. After a page load
on a site where manga mode is on, the reader opens by itself on chapter
pages (pages with the chapter images and a chapter button).

The page script (res/raw/cromiko_manga.js) runs in an isolated world of
the main frame through a small JNI bridge, CromikoPageScripts. The
configuration of each site is kept in the cromiko_manga_mode shared
preferences.

